{"title": "Quant Super Practice — Mock #175", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Which of the following equation has equal and positive roots?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["y<sup>2</sup>  -  10y + 16 = 0", "9y<sup>2</sup>  -  105y + 196 = 0", "9y<sup>2</sup>  -  24y + 16 = 0", "4y<sup>2</sup>  -  100y + 225 = 0"], "options_hi": ["y<sup>2</sup> - 10y + 16 = 0", "9y<sup>2</sup> - 105y + 196 = 0", "9y<sup>2</sup> - 24y + 16 = 0", "4y<sup>2</sup> - 100y + 225 = 0"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>From option (1):</p><p>For quadratic equation: y<sup>2</sup>  -  10y + 16 = 0</p><p>y<sup>2</sup>  -  10y + 16 = 0</p><p>y<sup>2</sup>  -  8y  -  2y + 16 = 0</p><p>y = 8, 2</p><p>Hence, roots of the given equation are positive but not equal.</p><p>From option (2):</p><p>For quadratic equation: 9y<sup>2</sup>  -  105y + 196 = 0</p><p>9y<sup>2</sup>  -  105y + 196 = 0</p><p>9y<sup>2</sup>  -  21y  -  84y + 196 = 0</p><p>y = 7/3, 28/3</p><p>Hence, roots of this equation are positive but not equal.</p><p>From option (3):</p><p>For quadratic equation: 9y<sup>2</sup>  -  24y + 16 = 0</p><p>9y<sup>2</sup>  -  24y + 16 = 0</p><p>9y<sup>2</sup>  -  12y  -  12y + 16 = 0</p><p>y = 4/3, 4/3</p><p>Hence, roots of this equation are positive and equal.</p><p>From option (4):</p><p>For quadratic equation: 4y<sup>2</sup>  -  100y + 225 = 0</p><p>4y<sup>2</sup>  -  100y + 225 = 0</p><p>4y<sup>2</sup>  -  90y  -  10y + 225 = 0</p><p>y = 45/2, 5/2</p><p>Hence, roots of this equation are positive but not equal.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>From option (1):</p><p>For quadratic equation: y<sup>2</sup>  -  10y + 16 = 0</p><p>y<sup>2</sup>  -  10y + 16 = 0</p><p>y<sup>2</sup>  -  8y  -  2y + 16 = 0</p><p>y = 8, 2</p><p>Hence, roots of the given equation are positive but not equal.</p><p>From option (2):</p><p>For quadratic equation: 9y<sup>2</sup>  -  105y + 196 = 0</p><p>9y<sup>2</sup>  -  105y + 196 = 0</p><p>9y<sup>2</sup>  -  21y  -  84y + 196 = 0</p><p>y = 7/3, 28/3</p><p>Hence, roots of this equation are positive but not equal.</p><p>From option (3):</p><p>For quadratic equation: 9y<sup>2</sup>  -  24y + 16 = 0</p><p>9y<sup>2</sup>  -  24y + 16 = 0</p><p>9y<sup>2</sup>  -  12y  -  12y + 16 = 0</p><p>y = 4/3, 4/3</p><p>Hence, roots of this equation are positive and equal.</p><p>From option (4):</p><p>For quadratic equation: 4y<sup>2</sup>  -  100y + 225 = 0</p><p>4y<sup>2</sup>  -  100y + 225 = 0</p><p>4y<sup>2</sup>  -  90y  -  10y + 225 = 0</p><p>y = 45/2, 5/2</p><p>Hence, roots of this equation are positive but not equal.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If a and b are roots of quadratic equation x<sup>2</sup>  -  22x + 85 = 0 and a &gt; b, then how many numbers between 100 and 1500 are divisible by both (a  -  b) and average of a and b?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a &#2324;&#2352; b &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2328;&#2366;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; x<sup>2</sup> - 22x + 85 = 0 &#2324;&#2352; a &gt; b &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; 100 &#2324;&#2352; 1500 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; (a - b) &#2324;&#2352; a &#2324;&#2352; b &#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["9", "11", "15", "17"], "options_hi": ["9", "11", "15", "17"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  22x + 85 = 0</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  17x  -  5x + 85 = 0</p><p>x = 17, 5</p><p>a = 17, b = 5</p><p>a  -  b = 17  -  5 = 12</p><p>Average of a and b = (17 + 5)/2 = 11</p><p>Numbers divisible by both 12 and 11 = numbers divisible by LCM of 12 and 11</p><p>LCM of 12 and 11 = 132</p><p>Numbers between 100 and 1500 which are divisible by 132 = 132, 264,...., 1452.</p><p>Total numbers = ((1452  -  132)/1320 + 1 = 11</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  22x + 85 = 0</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  17x  -  5x + 85 = 0</p><p>x = 17, 5</p><p>a = 17, b = 5</p><p>a  -  b = 17  -  5 = 12</p><p>Average of a and b = (17 + 5)/2 = 11</p><p>Numbers divisible by both 12 and 11 = numbers divisible by LCM of 12 and 11</p><p>LCM of 12 and 11 = 132</p><p>Numbers between 100 and 1500 which are divisible by 132 = 132, 264,...., 1452.</p><p>Total numbers = ((1452  -  132)/1320 + 1 = 11</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If one root of the equation 2x<sup>2</sup> + kx + m = 0 is 3 and (k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2</sup>  -  25<sup>2</sup>) =  - 15 such that m &gt; 0, then the other root is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; 2x<sup>2</sup> + kx + m = 0 &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; 3 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; (k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2</sup> - 25<sup>2</sup>) = - 15 &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367; m &gt; 0 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["7", "5", "7/2", "15/2"], "options_hi": ["7", "5", "7/2", "15/2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>As 3 is a root, so x = 3</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup> + kx + m = 0</p><p>18 + 3k + m = 0</p><p>m =  - (18 + 3k) .. (i)</p><p>(k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2</sup>  -  25<sup>2</sup>) =  - 15</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2 </sup>= 625  -  15 = 610</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + (18 + 3k)<sup>2 </sup>= 610</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + 324 + 108k + 9k<sup>2 </sup>= 610</p><p>10k<sup>2</sup> + 108k  -  286 = 0</p><p>5k<sup>2</sup> + 54k  -  143 = 0</p><p>k = 2.2 or  - 13</p><p>m =  - 24.6 or 21</p><p>As m &gt; 0, so k =  - 13 and m = 21</p><p>Hence, the equation is 2x<sup>2</sup>  -  13x + 21 = 0</p><p>So, solving we get that the other root is 7/2.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>As 3 is a root, so x = 3</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup> + kx + m = 0</p><p>18 + 3k + m = 0</p><p>m =  - (18 + 3k) .. (i)</p><p>(k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2</sup>  -  25<sup>2</sup>) =  - 15</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + m<sup>2 </sup>= 625  -  15 = 610</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + (18 + 3k)<sup>2 </sup>= 610</p><p>k<sup>2</sup> + 324 + 108k + 9k<sup>2 </sup>= 610</p><p>10k<sup>2</sup> + 108k  -  286 = 0</p><p>5k<sup>2</sup> + 54k  -  143 = 0</p><p>k = 2.2 or  - 13</p><p>m =  - 24.6 or 21</p><p>As m &gt; 0, so k =  - 13 and m = 21</p><p>Hence, the equation is 2x<sup>2</sup>  -  13x + 21 = 0</p><p>So, solving we get that the other root is 7/2.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If K and L are roots of the equation <img width=135 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image003.png\"> and K + L = 10, then what is the value of <img width=41 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image004.png\">?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; K &#2324;&#2352; L &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; K + L = 10 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["-10/19", "-5/38", "10/19", "5/38"], "options_hi": ["-10/19", "-5/38", "10/19", "5/38"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=228 height=145 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image005.png\"></p><p>Sum of the roots = K + L = 5p</p><p>Thus, K + L = 10</p><p>=&gt; 5p = 10</p><p>=&gt; p = 2</p><p>And KL = -19p<sup>2</sup> = -19 * 4</p><p><img width=203 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image006.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=228 height=145 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image005.png\"></p><p>Sum of the roots = K + L = 5p</p><p>Thus, K + L = 10</p><p>=&gt; 5p = 10</p><p>=&gt; p = 2</p><p>And KL = -19p<sup>2</sup> = -19 * 4</p><p><img width=203 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image006.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If the roots of the equations <img width=253 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image009.png\"> are equal, then what is the value of k?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; k &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1/2", "-1/2", "1", "-1"], "options_hi": ["1/2", "-1/2", "1", "-1"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=253 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image009.png\"></p><p>=&gt; (x + 1)[x(x  -  1)k  -  k(k + 1)] = x(x  -  1)(x + 1)(k  -  1)</p><p>=&gt; x(x  -  1)k  -  x(x  -  1)(k  -  1)  -  k(k + 1) = 0</p><p>=&gt; x(x  -  1)[k  -  k + 1]  -  k(k + 1) = 0</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup>  -  x  -  k(k + 1) = 0</p><p>Since, roots are equal.</p><p>Thus, b<sup>2</sup>  -  4ac = 0</p><p>=&gt; 1  -  4(-k(k + 1) = 0</p><p>=&gt; k(k + 1) = -1/4</p><p>=&gt; k<sup>2</sup> + k + &#188; = 0</p><p>=&gt; 4k<sup>2</sup> + 4k + 1 = 0</p><p>=&gt; (2k + 1)<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>=&gt; k = -1/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=253 height=43 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image009.png\"></p><p>=&gt; (x + 1)[x(x  -  1)k  -  k(k + 1)] = x(x  -  1)(x + 1)(k  -  1)</p><p>=&gt; x(x  -  1)k  -  x(x  -  1)(k  -  1)  -  k(k + 1) = 0</p><p>=&gt; x(x  -  1)[k  -  k + 1]  -  k(k + 1) = 0</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup>  -  x  -  k(k + 1) = 0</p><p>Since, roots are equal.</p><p>Thus, b<sup>2</sup>  -  4ac = 0</p><p>=&gt; 1  -  4(-k(k + 1) = 0</p><p>=&gt; k(k + 1) = -1/4</p><p>=&gt; k<sup>2</sup> + k + &#188; = 0</p><p>=&gt; 4k<sup>2</sup> + 4k + 1 = 0</p><p>=&gt; (2k + 1)<sup>2</sup> = 0</p><p>=&gt; k = -1/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Which one is one of the factors of <img width=169 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image016.png\">?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; <img width=169 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image016.png\"> &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["(3x + 2/x + 14)", "(2x + 3/x + 7)", "(2x + 3/x  -  5)", "(2x + 3/x  -  7)"], "options_hi": ["(3x + 2/x + 14)", "(2x + 3/x + 7)", "(2x + 3/x - 5)", "(2x + 3/x - 7)"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=319 height=196 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image017.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=319 height=196 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13823/image017.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the common factors in the equation (2p<sup>2</sup> + 11p - 63) and (24p<sup>2</sup> - 74p - 35).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; (2p<sup>2</sup> + 11p - 63) &#2324;&#2352; (24p<sup>2</sup> - 74p - 35) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2325; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3p - 8", "p + 9", "12p + 5", "2p - 7"], "options_hi": ["3p - 8", "p + 9", "12p + 5", "2p - 7"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>According to the Question,</p><p>Equation: (2p<sup>2</sup>+11p-63)</p><p>=2p<sup>2</sup>+18p-7p-63</p><p>=2p(p+9)-7(p+9)</p><p>=(2p-7) (p+9)</p><p>Equation: (24p<sup>2</sup>-74p-35)</p><p>=24p<sup>2</sup>-84p+10p-35</p><p>=12p(2p-7)+5(2p-7)</p><p>=(2p-7) (12p+5)</p><p>Common factor in both the equations is (2p-7)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the Question,</p><p>Equation: (2p<sup>2</sup>+11p-63)</p><p>=2p<sup>2</sup>+18p-7p-63</p><p>=2p(p+9)-7(p+9)</p><p>=(2p-7) (p+9)</p><p>Equation: (24p<sup>2</sup>-74p-35)</p><p>=24p<sup>2</sup>-84p+10p-35</p><p>=12p(2p-7)+5(2p-7)</p><p>=(2p-7) (12p+5)</p><p>Common factor in both the equations is (2p-7)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If 7/2 is one of roots of equation 2x<sup>2</sup>  -  px + 28 = 0. Find the other root of the equation and the value of p.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 7/2 &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; 2x<sup>2</sup> - px + 28 = 0 &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; p &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4, 13", "3/2, 15", "5, 15", "4, 15"], "options_hi": ["4, 13", "3/2, 15", "5, 15", "4, 15"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>If 7/2 is a root of the equation, then x = 7/2 will satisfy the equation</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup>  -  px + 28 = 0</p><p>2 * (7/2)<sup>2</sup>  -  p(7/2) + 28 = 0</p><p>49  -  7p + 56 = 0</p><p>7p = 105</p><p>p = 15</p><p>Equation = 2x<sup>2</sup>  -  15x + 28 = 0</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup>  -  (8 + 7)x + 28 = 0</p><p>(x  -  4)(2x  -  7) = 0</p><p>x = 4, 7/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If 7/2 is a root of the equation, then x = 7/2 will satisfy the equation</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup>  -  px + 28 = 0</p><p>2 * (7/2)<sup>2</sup>  -  p(7/2) + 28 = 0</p><p>49  -  7p + 56 = 0</p><p>7p = 105</p><p>p = 15</p><p>Equation = 2x<sup>2</sup>  -  15x + 28 = 0</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup>  -  (8 + 7)x + 28 = 0</p><p>(x  -  4)(2x  -  7) = 0</p><p>x = 4, 7/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>One root of the equation mx<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0 is 7/3. The value of m and the other root of equation respectively is - </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; mx<sup>2</sup> + 13x - 63 = 0 &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; 7/3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; m &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2361;&#2376; - </p>", "options_en": ["5, -9/2", "6, 9/2", "5, 9/2", "6, -9/2"], "options_hi": ["5, -9/2", "6, 9/2", "5, 9/2", "6, -9/2"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Since 7/3 is the root of equation mx<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0</p><p>m(7/3)<sup>2</sup> + 13*7/3  -  63 = 0</p><p>49m + 273  -  567 = 0</p><p>m = 294/49</p><p>m = 6</p><p>Now, equation: 6x<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0</p><p>Other root = (-63/6)/(7/3) = -9/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since 7/3 is the root of equation mx<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0</p><p>m(7/3)<sup>2</sup> + 13*7/3  -  63 = 0</p><p>49m + 273  -  567 = 0</p><p>m = 294/49</p><p>m = 6</p><p>Now, equation: 6x<sup>2</sup> + 13x  -  63 = 0</p><p>Other root = (-63/6)/(7/3) = -9/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following is a quadratic equation?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2328;&#2366;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["(x  -  5)(x + 3) = (x + 2)(x  -  12)", "(x + 5)<sup>2</sup> = x<sup>2</sup> + 7x - 6", "x<sup>3</sup>  -  4x<sup>2</sup>  -  x + 1 = (x  -  2)<sup>3</sup>", "(x + 3)<sup>3</sup> = 4x(x<sup>2</sup>  -  3)"], "options_hi": ["(x  -  5)(x + 3) = (x + 2)(x  -  12)", "(x + 5)<sup>2</sup> = x<sup>2</sup> + 7x - 6", "x<sup>3</sup>  -  4x<sup>2</sup>  -  x + 1 = (x  -  2)<sup>3</sup>", "(x + 3)<sup>3</sup> = 4x(x<sup>2</sup>  -  3)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>a) (x  -  5)(x + 3) = (x + 2)(x  -  12)</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  5x + 3x  -  15 = x<sup>2</sup> + 2x  -  12x  -  24</p><p>-2x  -  15 = - 10x  -  24</p><p>2x + 15 = 10x + 24</p><p>8x + 9 = 0(not quadratic equation)</p><p>b) (x + 5)<sup>2</sup> = x<sup>2</sup> + 7x - 6</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 25 + 10x = x<sup>2</sup> + 7x  -  6</p><p>3x + 31 = 0(not quadratic equation)</p><p>c) x<sup>3</sup>  -  4x<sup>2</sup>  -  x + 1 = (x  -  2)<sup>3</sup></p><p>x<sup>3</sup>  -  4x<sup>2</sup>  -  x + 1 = x<sup>3</sup>  -  8  -  6x<sup>2</sup> + 12x</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup>  -  13x + 9 = 0 (quadratic equation)</p><p>d) (x + 3)<sup>3</sup> = 4x(x<sup>2</sup>  -  3)</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> + 27 + 9x<sup>2</sup> + 27x = 4x<sup>3</sup>  -  12x</p><p>3x<sup>3</sup>  -  9x<sup>2</sup>  -  39x  -  27 = 0 (not quadratic equation)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a) (x  -  5)(x + 3) = (x + 2)(x  -  12)</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  5x + 3x  -  15 = x<sup>2</sup> + 2x  -  12x  -  24</p><p>-2x  -  15 = - 10x  -  24</p><p>2x + 15 = 10x + 24</p><p>8x + 9 = 0(not quadratic equation)</p><p>b) (x + 5)<sup>2</sup> = x<sup>2</sup> + 7x - 6</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 25 + 10x = x<sup>2</sup> + 7x  -  6</p><p>3x + 31 = 0(not quadratic equation)</p><p>c) x<sup>3</sup>  -  4x<sup>2</sup>  -  x + 1 = (x  -  2)<sup>3</sup></p><p>x<sup>3</sup>  -  4x<sup>2</sup>  -  x + 1 = x<sup>3</sup>  -  8  -  6x<sup>2</sup> + 12x</p><p>2x<sup>2</sup>  -  13x + 9 = 0 (quadratic equation)</p><p>d) (x + 3)<sup>3</sup> = 4x(x<sup>2</sup>  -  3)</p><p>x<sup>3</sup> + 27 + 9x<sup>2</sup> + 27x = 4x<sup>3</sup>  -  12x</p><p>3x<sup>3</sup>  -  9x<sup>2</sup>  -  39x  -  27 = 0 (not quadratic equation)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If (3x + 7) and (2x + 3) both are factors of px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q = 0, then</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (3x + 7) &#2324;&#2352; (2x + 3) &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q = 0 &#2325;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379;</p>", "options_en": ["p = (3 + q)/4", "3p = q + 5", "3p = q  -  3", "2p = q"], "options_hi": ["p = (3 + q)/4", "3p = q + 5", "3p = q  -  3", "2p = q"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>According to question,</p><p>(3x + 7)(2x + 3) = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>6x<sup>2</sup> + 14x + 9x + 21 = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>6x<sup>2 </sup>+ 23x + 21 = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>Comparing both sides we get,</p><p>p = 6, q = 21</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to question,</p><p>(3x + 7)(2x + 3) = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>6x<sup>2</sup> + 14x + 9x + 21 = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>6x<sup>2 </sup>+ 23x + 21 = px<sup>2</sup> + 23x + q</p><p>Comparing both sides we get,</p><p>p = 6, q = 21</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>If one of the roots of a quadratic equation is (8 - 7&radic;5), then find the quadratic equation. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2328;&#2366;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; (8 - 7&radic;5) &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2328;&#2366;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["X<sup>2</sup> + 16X + 181 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup>  -  16X  -  309 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup> + 16X + 309 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup>  -  16X  -  181 = 0"], "options_hi": ["X<sup>2</sup> + 16X + 181 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup>  -  16X  -  309 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup> + 16X + 309 = 0", "X<sup>2</sup>  -  16X  -  181 = 0"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The one root of quadratic equation = 8 - 7&radic;5</p><p><b>We know that:</b> Irrational roots always occur in pairs.</p><p>Then, the other root of the quadratic equation = 8 + 7&radic;5</p><p>So, the required equation = [X  -  (8 - 7&radic;5)] * [X  -  (8 + 7&radic;5)] = X<sup>2</sup>  -  16X  -  181 = 0</p>", "solution_h